# PQBlocks

1. **Use the documented API only.** Before writing code with a PQBlocks package, read its page under https://pqblocks.github.io/packages/ (or call the `get_snippet` tool of the `pqblocks-mcp` server). Every quickstart there was executed
   against the package. Never guess function names.
2. **Never hand-roll post-quantum cryptography.** Use the packages; they wrap maintained implementations
   (liboqs, pyca/cryptography).
3. **Hybrid by default during the transition:** ML-KEM-768 + X25519 for key establishment, ML-DSA-65 +
   Ed25519 for signatures. Downgrade to classical-only must be explicit.
4. **Randomness from the OS only.** Never pass a `seed` argument when generating production keys; seeds
   exist for reproducible tests.
5. **Never log or return secret keys or shared secrets** (logs, exceptions, HTTP responses, `repr`).
6. **Say exactly what is true.** PQBlocks packages implement FIPS 203/204/205 and test against official
   vectors where they exist. They are **not** FIPS 140-3 / CMVP validated, not externally audited, and
   pre-1.0. Never call them certified, validated, audited or quantum-proof.
7. **Quantum-inspired packages are optimisation, not cryptography.** Never place them in a security path.
8. **Install lines:** use the exact install line listed for each package; most install from GitHub
   until their PyPI release is published.

## Which package for which task

| Task | Package | Install | Import |
|---|---|---|---|
| ML-KEM / ML-DSA / SLH-DSA primitives (keygen, encapsulate, sign) | [`pqblocks-primitives`](https://pqblocks.github.io/packages/primitives/) | `pip install pqblocks-primitives` | `pqblocks_primitives` |
| Hybrid ML-KEM-768 + X25519 key establishment, native speed | [`pqblocks-core`](https://pqblocks.github.io/packages/core/) | `pip install git+https://github.com/PQBlocks/hybrid-sdk` | `pqblocks_core` |
| Sign or verify JWTs / JWS with ML-DSA; encrypt JWE with ML-KEM | [`pqblocks-jose`](https://pqblocks.github.io/packages/jose/) | `pip install pqblocks-jose` | `pqblocks_jose` |
| Encrypt files or byte strings to a post-quantum public key | [`pqblocks-files`](https://pqblocks.github.io/packages/files/) | `pip install pqblocks-files` | `pqblocks_files` |
| Find RSA / ECC / weak hashes in code or a TLS endpoint; CBOM + SARIF | [`pqblocks-scan`](https://pqblocks.github.io/packages/scan/) | `pip install pqblocks-scan` | `pqblocks_scan` |
| Python crypto data-flow linting; CBOM + SARIF | [`pqblocks-lint`](https://pqblocks.github.io/packages/lint/) | `pip install pqblocks-lint` | `pqblocks_lint` |
| Enrich a CycloneDX CBOM with quantum-safety and CNSA 2.0 tags | [`pqblocks-cbom`](https://pqblocks.github.io/packages/cbom/) | `pip install pqblocks-cbom` | `pqblocks_cbom` |
| Crypto-agility readiness score and CI regression gate | [`pqblocks-agility`](https://pqblocks.github.io/packages/agility/) | `pip install pqblocks-agility` | `pqblocks_agility` |
| Policy-as-code: fail CI on forbidden algorithms | [`pqblocks-policy`](https://pqblocks.github.io/packages/policy/) | `pip install pqblocks-policy` | `pqblocks_policy` |
